{"from": "passage:mk-15-01", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-01", "note": "The council's morning consultation, binding Jesus and delivering him to Pilate."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-02", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-11", "note": "Pilate's question 'Are you the King of the Jews?' and 'So you say.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-03", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-12", "note": "The chief priests' accusations before the governor."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-13", "note": "Pilate's question about the many things testified against him."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-05", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-14", "note": "Jesus' silence to every charge, so that the governor marveled."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-06", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-15", "note": "The governor's custom of releasing one prisoner at the feast."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-07", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-16", "note": "The prisoner called Barabbas (Mark adds the insurrection detail)."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-08", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-21", "note": "The multitude crying out and asking for a release."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-09", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-17", "note": "Pilate asks the crowd whether to release the King of the Jews."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-10", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-18", "note": "Pilate perceived that it was for envy the chief priests had delivered him up."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-11", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-20", "note": "The chief priests stirring up the multitude to ask for Barabbas."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-12", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-22", "note": "Pilate's 'What then shall I do?' and the crowd's 'Crucify him!'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-13", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-22", "note": "The crowd crying out 'Crucify him!'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-14", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-23", "note": "Pilate's 'What evil has he done?' and the repeated cry."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-26", "note": "Barabbas released; Jesus flogged and handed over to be crucified."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-16", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-27", "note": "The soldiers take him into the praetorium and gather the whole cohort/garrison."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-17", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-28", "note": "The robe: Mark's purple cloak against Matthew's scarlet robe."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-18", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-29", "note": "The mock salutation 'Hail, King of the Jews!'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-19", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-30", "note": "Striking his head with a reed and spitting on him."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-20", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-31", "note": "Robe removed, own garments replaced, led out to crucify him."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-32", "note": "Simon of Cyrene compelled to carry the cross."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-22", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-33", "note": "The place called Golgotha, 'the place of a skull'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-23", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-34", "note": "The drugged wine offered and refused (Mark: myrrh; Matthew: gall)."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-24", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-35", "note": "Crucified; garments divided by casting lots."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-25", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-35", "note": "The crucifixion itself; Mark alone dates it 'the third hour'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-26", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-37", "note": "The written charge over him: 'THE KING OF THE JEWS'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-27", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-38", "note": "Two robbers crucified with him, one on the right and one on the left."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-29", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-39", "note": "Those passing by reviling him, wagging their heads."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-30", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-40", "note": "'You who destroy the temple and build it in three days; save yourself.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-41", "note": "The chief priests and scribes mocking: 'He saved others; himself he cannot save.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-32", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-42", "note": "'Let the Christ, the King of Israel, come down now from the cross.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-33", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-45", "note": "Darkness over the whole land from the sixth to the ninth hour."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-34", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-46", "note": "The cry 'My God, my God, why have you forsaken me' (Mark: Eloi; Matthew: Eli)."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-35", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-47", "note": "The bystanders: 'He is calling Elijah.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-36", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-48", "note": "The sponge of vinegar on a reed and 'Let him be; let us see whether Elijah comes.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-37", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-50", "note": "Jesus crying with a loud voice and yielding up his spirit."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-38", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-51", "note": "The veil of the temple torn in two from top to bottom."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-39", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-54", "note": "The centurion's 'Truly this man was the Son of God!'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-40", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-55", "note": "Women watching from afar, Mary Magdalene among them."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-41", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-56", "note": "Mary the mother of James and Joses; Mark names Salome where Matthew names the mother of the sons of Zebedee."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-42", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-57", "note": "Evening on Preparation Day; Matthew's day-after-Preparation guard scene follows."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-43", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-57", "note": "Joseph of Arimathea going to Pilate for the body."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-44", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-58", "note": "Pilate and the request for the body; Mark adds the centurion inquiry."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-45", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-58", "note": "Pilate grants the body."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-46", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-59", "note": "Wrapping the body and laying it in a rock-cut tomb."}
{"from": "passage:mk-15-47", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-27-61", "note": "Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joses seeing where he was laid."}
