{"from": "text:josephus-war-4-317-burial", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-15-44-45-body-release", "grade": "C", "note": "War 4.317: in the 70 CE siege 'they took down those that were condemned and crucified, and buried them before the going down of the sun' - the standing Jerusalem practice of burying the executed that the release for burial presupposes; wartime practice a generation later, so C."}
{"from": "artifact:yehohanan-heel-bone", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-15-44-45-body-release", "grade": "C", "note": "Yehohanan, a crucified man buried by his family in an ossuary at Giv'at ha-Mivtar - it shows a crucified man received burial, not Pilate's verification-and-grant procedure itself, so C."}
